35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The receipts show 2,300 yen monthly, often duplicated. The management office charges 4,200 yen per hour.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"A full pass takes 102 minutes. Standards vary wildly; some stop at the basin, others clean the drain.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The kitchen mess comes from three people. Two of us are away most months. The work doesn't match the presence.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,The grout is black again in eleven days. The chat shows our fights start with reminders about undone tasks.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,The previous tenants split rooms permanently and stopped speaking. The outside firm requires us to tidy first.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, 102 minutes is significant. If we hire out, the cost is high, but the time is saved.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, yes. But if we do it ourselves, the inconsistency in ""done"" is the real problem.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, the grout issue suggests the bathroom is a losing battle for us. The kitchen is where the real load is.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, exactly. I can't keep bracing for the bathroom. I need a system that handles the decay.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Toshio, the previous tenants' silence is a warning. Permanent assignments might isolate us.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"The financials are clear. 2,300 yen is manageable. 4,200 yen per hour is steep but predictable.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,The time is the killer. 102 minutes is a large chunk of my week. I need to know if I can delegate it.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"The usage data is damning. Three people cook, two are away. A fixed rota ignores this reality.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"The chat logs prove that ambiguity causes conflict. We need clear, non-negotiable standards or external help.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"The firm's terms mean we still have to tidy. It's not a full hand-off. But it removes the ""who did it"" argument.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I am leaning towards the paid service. It removes the financial ambiguity and the time burden.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. The time savings are worth the cost. The inconsistency in standards makes DIY risky.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I am hesitant. The firm requires us to tidy. But the usage imbalance makes a rota unfair.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,I prefer the paid service. It solves the bathroom decay and the kitchen unpredictability.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I am worried about the ""tidy beforehand"" clause. But it might be better than the previous tenants' silence.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
